            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Thom Hoffenkamp"
            },
            "reviewBody": "When making it for the first time, it worried me. It's like a soup at first. Doesn't seem to match the descriptive words like \"spread\" in the recipe. It should say \"pour\" the batter into the baking pan. Same with the rhubarb mix. Time will tell, I told myself...always trust Allrecipes. Turned out fantastic. Whole family loved it. Tips would be to plan to cook it slightly longer than the suggested 40 minutes to brown and finish the top, to match your preferred result. Delicious and instant family favorite. Even before finishing their first serving, my kids were suggesting we bring it to family gatherings year-round! So glad I planted rhubarb this year!",
